        "text": "{\"id\":\"SFN-17\",\"title\":\"Build MailFn as a reusable programmable mailbox function\",\"description\":\"## Executive summary\\n\\nCapture the initial product and architecture direction for MailFn: a standalone, reusable Superfunctions capability for programmable mailboxes and inbound email workflows across Router and other projects.\\n\\nMailFn should begin as a focused, self-deployable mailbox runtime and preserve a clear boundary with SendFn. MailFn owns stateful inbox identities, inbound messages, retrieval, testing primitives, and mailbox lifecycle. SendFn remains responsible for outbound delivery and notification orchestration.\\n\\n## Problem or opportunity\\n\\nProjects that automate acquisition, authentication, QA, and agent workflows need controlled email identities that can receive verification codes, magic links, lifecycle messages, and attachments through an API. Implementing this independently in each project would duplicate infrastructure, security controls, storage, and agent integrations.\\n\\nSuperfunctions already provides shared foundations and an outbound communications function, making a reusable MailFn domain a natural extension.\\n\\n## Expected outcome\\n\\nA validated MailFn product boundary and phased delivery plan that supports:\\n\\n* reusable deployment outside Router;\\n* stable and expiring inbox identities;\\n* Cloudflare-based inbound email processing;\\n* agent-safe message retrieval and waiting;\\n* a provider-neutral core with platform adapters;\\n* composition with SendFn for outbound send and reply behavior;\\n* a credible path from test inboxes to durable mailbox functionality.\\n\\n## Goals\\n\\n* Define MailFn as an independently publishable Superfunctions domain.\\n* Establish clear MailFn, SendFn, TestFn, and shared-package boundaries.\\n* Design a minimal inbound-first release suitable for verification and lifecycle workflows.\\n* Support SDK, CLI, and MCP access with scoped credentials.\\n* Preserve raw evidence while applying explicit retention and secret-handling controls.\\n* Keep the architecture reusable across multiple products and projects.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n\\n* Implement MailFn as part of this backlog-capture task.\\n* Replace SendFn's outbound delivery responsibilities.\\n* Launch a public arbitrary-recipient outbound email service in the initial release.\\n* Commit to dates, staffing, pricing, or production availability.\\n* Build a complete webmail client in the initial release.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] The MailFn ownership boundary relative to SendFn and TestFn is documented and approved.\\n- [ ] A provider-neutral core contract is defined for inboxes, messages, attachments, threads, scoped credentials, storage, and inbound transports.\\n- [ ] A Cloudflare deployment design covers Email Routing, Workers, D1, R2, Queues, DNS, and failure handling.\\n- [ ] The initial API covers stable and expiring inboxes, list/read/wait operations, filtering, OTP and verification-link extraction, retention, and revocation.\\n- [ ] TypeScript SDK, CLI, and MCP surfaces are specified with least-privilege defaults.\\n- [ ] Security covers OTP secrecy, credential scoping, webhook verification, idempotency, unknown-recipient rejection, retention, deletion, rate limits, and auditability.\\n- [ ] Send/reply functionality is composed through SendFn rather than duplicated.\\n- [ ] Testing covers MIME parsing, concurrent verification messages, attachments, retries, expiry, authorization boundaries, and Cloudflare failure modes.\\n- [ ] A phased roadmap distinguishes the initial internal capability from later durable mailbox and public-platform functionality.\\n- [ ] Release integration covers explicit workspace registration, package publication metadata, scoped CI, and a dedicated release gate.\\n\\n## Dependencies and risks\\n\\n* Cloudflare Email Routing and Worker runtime behavior.\\n* D1, R2, and Queue storage and delivery semantics.\\n* Existing SendFn and shared delivery contracts on the Superfunctions next branch.\\n* Explicit Superfunctions workspace and release-target registration.\\n* Sensitive authentication content requires strict logging and retention controls.\\n* Public outbound capability would introduce substantial abuse, reputation, suppression, and compliance responsibilities.\\n* Default or newly created domains may be rejected by some products.\\n* Existing Superfunctions worktrees contain unrelated changes; implementation should use a dedicated worktree.\\n\\n## Open questions\\n\\n* Should the initial package family use `@mailfn/core` plus adapters, an unscoped `mailfn` facade, or both?\\n* Should the first release be internal-only or generally publishable?\\n* What are the default message and attachment retention periods?\\n* Which APIs belong in MailFn versus an optional testing package?\\n* Should OTP and verification-link extraction occur in the service, SDK, or MCP layer?\\n* What tenancy boundary should separate projects and environments?\\n* Which outbound operations, if any, are required for the first release?\\n* What security and operational gates must be satisfied before custom-domain or public use?\\n\\n## Supporting documents\\n\\n* [Ideation & Product Rationale — SFN-17: Build MailFn as a reusable programmable mailbox function](<https://linear.app/21n/document/ideation-and-product-rationale-sfn-17-build-mailfn-as-a-reusable-a98720d95595>)\\n* [Architecture & Delivery Plan — SFN-17: Build MailFn as a reusable programmable mailbox function](<https://linear.app/21n/document/architecture-and-delivery-plan-sfn-17-build-mailfn-as-a-reusable-f9905e68e72e>)\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/21n/issue/SFN-17/build-mailfn-as-a-reusable-programmable-mailbox-function\",\"gitBranchName\":\"aravink/sfn-17-build-mailfn-as-a-reusable-programmable-mailbox-function\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-10T07:58:54.276Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-10T08:01:58.975Z\",\"archivedAt\":null,\"completedAt\":null,\"startedAt\":null,\"canceledAt\":null,\"dueDate\":null,\"slaStartedAt\":null,\"slaMediumRiskAt\":null,\"slaHighRiskAt\":null,\"slaBreachesAt\":null,\"status\":\"Backlog\",\"statusType\":\"backlog\",\"labels\":[],\"attachments\":[],\"documents\":[{\"id\":\"3327d5f1-6e0b-45b9-bcde-bc1524faa801\",\"title\":\"Ideation & Product Rationale — SFN-17: Build MailFn as a reusable programmable mailbox function\"},{\"id\":\"2a30481e-7e19-45a3-8c7c-2ae1e030dfc4\",\"title\":\"Architecture & Delivery Plan — SFN-17: Build MailFn as a reusable programmable mailbox function\"}],\"stateHistory\":[{\"state\":{\"id\":\"85023df2-b48b-42ee-b4b4-fe32f00e6c23\",\"name\":\"Backlog\",\"type\":\"backlog\"},\"startedAt\":\"2026-08-10T07:58:54.276Z\",\"endedAt\":null}],\"createdBy\":\"Aravind\",\"createdById\":\"3a6ed003-6380-47ef-9e7b-b2b01ebddc6a\",\"team\":\"SF Next\",\"teamId\":\"8ce97d01-cdf7-47e4-a213-c3dbddc86d63\",\"relations\":{\"blocks\":[],\"blockedBy\":[],\"relatedTo\":[],\"duplicateOf\":null}}"
